# Read Text File using Python

## Aim
To read the contents of a text file using different file handling methods in Python.

## Description
This program demonstrates three methods of reading a text file:
1. readline() - Reads one line at a time.
2. readlines() - Reads all lines and stores them in a list.
3. read() - Reads the entire file content as a string.

## File Used
test.txt

## Execution
Run the program using:

```bash
python3 read_txtfile.py
```

## Output
The program displays the contents of test.txt using readline(), readlines(), and read() methods.

## Concepts Used
- Python File Handling
- Open and Close
- readline()
- readlines()
- read()
